# Leave website/ out of product work

`website/` is the public site used to describe Adlexone and ask for a copy. It is static HTML, CSS, and assets. It is not part of the application.

When the task is the application:

- Do not treat files under `website/` as product code.
- Do not add PHP, screens, classes, or routes there.
- Do not wire the application to serve `website/`.
- Do not include `website/` in a release. `bin/build-release.php` leaves that folder out, and the root `.htaccess` refuses it.
- Point product searches at `src/`, `layouts/`, `bootstrap/`, and `public/`.

Work in `website/` only when the task is the sales site. Keep that copy in the same voice as the product.
